cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IAClassLibrary in your work, please cite the software as below."
title: "IAClassLibrary: Image Analysis Class Library"
abstract: >-
  IAClassLibrary is a reusable Java library of image-processing and
  analysis primitives for the ImageJ/Fiji ecosystem. It is consumed as a
  dependency by ADAPT, TrackerLibrary, and AdaptDataProcessing, providing
  cell and particle models, a multi-threaded processing pipeline,
  Bio-Formats image loading, segmentation, and statistics/optimisation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Barry
    given-names: David J
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2763-5244"
    affiliation: "The Francis Crick Institute, London, UK"
repository-code: "https://github.com/djpbarry/IAClassLibrary"
url: "https://djpbarry.github.io/IAClassLibrary/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - image analysis
  - microscopy
  - ImageJ
  - Fiji
  - segmentation
  - cell migration
  - Bio-Formats
